<div class="cq ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c8"><span class="c4">WHEREAS the father of the Vendor no.1 herein late Dhan Singh having share in the land in Sy.No.127, 129, 130, 133, 134, 145, 147, 148 &amp; 149 total admeasuring Ac.21 : 19 guntas, situated at Puppalguda Village, Rajendra Nagar Mandal, presently in Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District, Telangana State.</span></div>
<div class="cr ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ci"><span class="c4">&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;WHEREAS&#160; late Dhan Singh during his life time filed a suit for partition and separate possession claiming in the&#160; respect of land in Sy.127, 129, 130, 133, 134, 145, 147, 148 &amp; 149 admeasuring Ac.21 : 19 guntas,&#160; situated at Puppalguda Village, presently in Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District, vide O.S.No.473 of 2000 on the file of Hon'ble IV Additional Senior Civil Judge (FTC), Ranga Reddy District at&#160; L.B. Nagar against the Satyanarayana Singh and Ramesh Singh and the said suit was&#160; dismissed in the year 2009.&#160; &#160;after due contest Aggrieved by the said Judgment Dhan Singh preferred appeal before the Hon&#8217;ble High Court of Telangana vide A.S.No.552 of 2009.&#160; During pending of the appeal Dhan Singh, Satyanarayana Singh and Ramesh Singh were died and their legal heirs have brought on record and thereafter due to the intervention of the family elders and well-wishers the matter has been settled between the parties amicably and accordingly all the parties entered into a memorandum of compromise dated 14-08-2020 and the same has been filed in A.S.No.552 of 2009 before the Hon&#8217;ble High Court of Telangana in the compromise the vendor No.1 along with his brothers Arjun Singh and Sudheer Singh herein got the land admeasuring Ac.05:17 guntas out of the total extent of land admeasuring Ac.21:19 guntas, in Sy.Nos 127, 129, 130, 133, 134, 145, 147, 148 &amp; 149 situated at Puppalguda Village, Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District.</span></div>
<div class="ci"><span class="c4">WHEREAS late Satyanarayana Singh during the pendency of the partition suit vide O.S.No.473 of 2000 entered into a Registered deed of Exchange vide Doct.no.9130 of 2004 dated 29-11-2004 with Mr. B. Vijay and four others, who are the owners of the land in Sy.No.128/1, admeasuring Ac.1 : 02 guntas, situated at Puppalguda Village, Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District, purchased the said land in the Auction conducted by the Government vide proceedings no.LC2/7279/2003 dated 20-09-2003.&#160; In the said exchange deed late Satyanarayana Singh had exchanged the land by giving the land admeasuring Ac.00 : 15.5 guntas, out of his share of land admeasuring Ac.00 : 18 guntas in Sy.No.127, situated at Puppalguda Village, Rajendra Nagar Mandal, presently in Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District, by taking the land admeasuring Ac.00:15.5 guntas, out of Ac.01:02 guntas, in Sy.No.128/1, situated at Puppalguda Village, Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District with the distinct boundaries. </span></div>
<div class="cs ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c8"><span class="c4">WHEREAS late Satyanarayana Singh also entered into another deed of exchange vide Doc.No.57 of 2006 dated 02-01-2006 with one K.Rama Krishna Reddy S/o. K.Ram Reddy by exchanging the land by giving 597 Sq. Yards of land in Sy.No.127, 129 and 130 situated at Puppalguda Village, Rajendra Nagar Mandal, presently in Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District by taking the land admeasuring 600 Sy.yards, in Sy.No.128/3, situated at Puppalguda Village, Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District with the distinct boundaries.</span></div>
