<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="c36"><span class="cj">GST:</span></div>
<div class="c37"><span class="c4">1.&#160; 5% on Sale Consideration</span></div></div>
<div class="c37"><span class="c4">2.&#160; 18% on Maintenance, Move in, legal &amp; documentation charges</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">Explanation:</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c39">(i)<span class="c38"></span><span class="c4">The Total Price above includes the booking amount paid by the VENDEE/S to the DEVELOPER towards the Flat;</span></div>
<div class="c3a ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c39">(ii)<span class="c3b"></span><span class="c4">The Total Price above includes taxes( consisting of tax paid or payable by the DEVELOPER by way of Cess or any other similar taxes which may be levied, in connection with the construction of the Project payable by the DEVELOPER, by whatever name called up to the date of handing over the possession of the flat to the Association and the project or the competent authority, as the case may be, after obtaining the completion certificate: Provided that in case there is any change/modification in taxes, the subsequent amount payable by the VENDEE to the DEVELOPER shall be increased/reduced based on such change/modification: Provided further that if there is any increase in the taxes after the expiry of the scheduled date of completion of the project as per registration with the Authority, which shall include the extension of registration, if any, granted to the said project by the Authority, as per the Act, the same shall not be charged from the VENDEE/S provided that Stamp Duty, Registration fee, mutation charges, shall be paid by the VENDEE/S as per actual over and above the total price. </span></div>
<div class="c3a ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c39">(iii)<span class="c3c"></span><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER shall periodically intimate in writing to the VENDEE/S, the amount payable as mentioned in Schedule C and the VENDEE/S shall make payment demanded by the DEVELOPER within the time and in the manner specified therein. </span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c39">(iv)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">The Total price of Flat includes undivided share price of land, construction of not only the Flat but also the Common areas, internal development charges, external development charges, taxes, cost of providing electric wiring, electrical connectivity to the flat, lift, Internal water line and plumbing, finishing with paint,&#160; doors, flooring, windows, fire detection and firefighting equipment (as per law) in the common areas, maintenance charges as per para 11, etc. and includes cost for providing all other facilities, amenities and specifications to be provided as per the agreement within the Flat and the Project;</span></div>
<div class="c3a ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.2<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4"> The VENDEE/S hereby agree to become a member of the Society or&#160; &#160; Association so formed by all the tenement owners of THE LEGACEY Project and the VENDEE/S agree to contribute 4/-. per sft for maintenance charges with 18% GST to the DEVELOPER and for Association for period of 2 years and which can be extendable and for Corpus fund 50/- per sft </span></div>
<div class="c3e ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.3<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4"> The Total Price is escalation-free, however, in case the VENDEE/S agree to pay the escalation charges is due to increase on account of development charges payable to the competent authority and/or any other increase in charges which may be levied or imposed by the competent authority from time to time. The DEVELOPER undertakes and agrees that while raising a demand on the VENDEE/S for increase in development charges, cost/charges, imposed by the competent authorities, the DEVELOPER shall enclose the said notification/order/charges imposed by the competent authorities, the DEVELOPER shall enclose the said notification/order/rule/regulation to that effect along with the demand letter being issued to the VENDEE/S.</span></div>
<div class="c3e ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.4<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4"> The VENDEE/S shall make the payment as per the payment plan as set out hereunder shall be as per Schedule &#8220;C&#8221; plan.</span></div>
<div class="c3f ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.5<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4"> The DEVELOPER may allow, in its sole discretion, a rebate for early payments of installments payable by the VENDEE/S by discounting such early payments 12% per annum for the period by which the respective installment has been prepone. The provision for allowing rebate and such rate of rebate shall not be subject to any revision/withdrawal, once granted to VENDEE/S by the DEVELOPER.</span></div>
<div class="c3f ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.6<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4">It is agreed that the DEVELOPER shall not make any additions and alterations in the sanctioned plans and specifications, with such modifications as may be been made by the Developer as may be deemed fit and in the nature of the Project and the nature of fixtures, fittings and amenities described herein in Schedule &#8216;D&#8217; in respect of the flat as the case may be, without the previous written consent of the VENDEE/S as per the provisions of the Act. Provided that the DEVELOPER may make such minor additions/deductions or alterations as may be required by the VENDEE/S, or such minor changes or alterations as per the provisions of the Act, on such terms as may be agreed without any deduction in the sales receivables to the DEVELOPER by the VENDEE/S. The DEVELOPER shall not be liable for any manufacturing or other defects of any branded inputs or fixtures or services of any third party mentioned in the schedule/annexure to this Agreement, unless it results in structural defects. The Association of VENDEE/S shall take responsibility for proper safety, maintenance (including continuance of annual maintenance/insurance contracts/agreements) and upkeep of all the fixtures, equipment and machinery provided by the DEVELOPER for which the DEVELOPER shall not be liable after handing over.</span></div>
<div class="co ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.7<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4">It is agreed between the parties that in the event of there being any modifications to the Floor Plan attached to this Agreement, the same shall be duly intimated to the Vendee by the Developer and the Vendee shall raise any objections to the same, within a period of 7 days from the date of such intimation after which period, it shall be deemed that the Vendee has accepted the modifications proposed.</span></div>
<div class="co ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.8<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER shall confirm to the final carpet and saleable area that has been allotted to the VENDEE/S after the construction of the Building is complete and the occupancy certificate is granted by the competent authority, by furnishing details of the changes, if any, in the built-up area or the Saleable area. The total price payable for the built up or saleable area shall be recalculated upon confirmation by the DEVELOPER. If there is reduction in the built-up area or the Saleable area then the DEVELOPER shall refund the excess money paid by the VENDEE/S within forty-five days with annual interest at the rate prescribed in the Rules, from the date when such an excess amount was paid by the VENDEE/S</span><span class="c5">. </span><span class="c4">If there is any increase in the built-up area or the Saleable area, which is not more than three percent of the built-up area of the flat, allotted to the VENDEE/S as per the next milestone of the Payment plan as provided in Schedule C. All these monetary adjustments shall be made at the same rate per square feet as agreed in para 1.1 of this Agreement.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.9<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4">Subject to para 9.3, the VENDEE/S agree and acknowledge, the VENDEE/S shall have the right to the Flat Schedule B Property as mentioned below subject the VENDEE/S making the payments as per schedule and on payment of total sale consideration.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c3g">(i)<span class="c38"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S shall have exclusive ownership of their respective schedule flat.</span></div>
<div class="c3h ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c3i">(ii)<span class="c3b"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S shall also have undivided proportionate share in the common areas. Since the share of the VENDEE/S in the common areas is undivided and cannot be divided or separated, the VENDEE/S shall use the common areas along with other occupants, maintenance staff, etc. without causing any inconvenience or hindrance to them. It is clarified that the DEVELOPER shall hand over the common areas to the Association of VENDEE/S after duly obtaining the completion certificate from the competent authority as provided in the Act;</span></div>
<div class="c3h ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c3i">(iii)<span class="c3c"></span><span class="c4">That the computation of the price of the flat includes recovery of price of land, construction of [not only the flat but also] the Common areas, internal development charges, external development charges, taxes, cost of providing electric wiring, electrical connectivity to the flat, lift, Internal water line and plumbing, finishing with paint, granite, tiles, doors, windows, fire detection and firefighting equipment (as per law) in the common areas, maintenance charges as per the agreement within the [Flat].</span></div>
<div class="c3h ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c3i">(iv)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S have the right to visit their Flat on prior intimation of at least 3 working days to the DEVELPOR / Authorized person to assess the extent of development of his /her Flat</span><span class="c5">. </span><span class="c4">It is made clear by the DEVELOPER and the VENDEE/S agree that the Flat Schedule B Property along with parking space treated as a single indivisible unit for all purposes. It is agreed that the Project is an independent, self-contained Project covering the said Land and is not a part of any other project or zone and shall not form a part of and/or linked/combined with any other project in its vicinity or otherwise except for the purpose of integration of infrastructure for the benefit of the VENDEE/S. It is clarified that Project&#8217;s facilities and amenities shall be available only for the use and enjoyment of the VENDEE/S of the Project.</span></div>
<div class="c3j ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.10<span class="c3k"></span><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER agrees to pay all outgoings before transferring the physical possession or transfer of Scheduled Property whichever is earlier, of the flat to the VENDEE/S, which it has collected from the VENDEE/S, for the payment of outgoings (including land cost [either directly or by way of share in the project, ground rent, municipal or other local taxes, charges for water or electricity, maintenance charges, including mortgage loan and interest on mortgages or other encumbrances and such other liabilities payable to competent authorities, banks and financial institutions, which are related to the project). If DEVELOPER fails to pay all or any of the outgoings collected by it from the VENDEE/S or any liability, mortgage loan and interest thereon before transferring the flat to the VENDEE/S or any liability, mortgage loan and interest thereon before transferring the flat to the VENDEE/S, the DEVELOPER agrees to be liable, even after the transfer of the property, to pay such outgoings and penal charges, if any, to the authority or person to whom they are payable and be liable for the cost of any legal proceedings which may be taken there for by such authority or persons.</span></div>
<div class="c3l ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.11<span class="c3m"></span><span class="c4"> VENDEE/S has paid </span><span class="c5">a sum of </span><span class="c7">Rs. {!formattedTotalReceivedFlatAmount}/- ({!totalReceivedFlatAmountInWords})</span><span class="c5"> </span><span class="c4">as booking amount, excluding GST being part payment towards the total price of the flat at the time of entering this Agreement, the receipt of which the DEVELOPER hereby acknowledges in the table below and the VENDEE/S hereby agrees to pay the remaining price of the flat as prescribed in the Payment Plan (Schedule C) as may be demanded by the DEVELOPER within the time and in the manner specified therein.</span></div>
