<div class="c3v ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.12<span class="c3k"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S shall pay the installments as stipulated above within 15 days from the date of notice issued by the DEVELOPER, failing which it shall carry interest at the rate of 24% prescribed in the Rules.</span></div>
<div class="c3w ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.13<span class="c3k"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S shall issue post-dated cheques for all installments as per the payment schedule given above irrespective of mode of funding, i.e. self/bank finance. The VENDEE/S unconditionally agree to sign the disbursement forms of respective banks in advance along with this agreement and handover such papers to the </span></div>
<div class="ci ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2y">1.14<span class="c3k"></span><span class="c4">DEVELOPER enabling the DEVELOPER to submit with respective banks for release of payments avoiding delay in releasing installment amounts without any hindrance and the DEVELOPER hereby undertakes and confirms to the VENDEE/S that the said disbursal from the Demand Letter from the DEVELOPER will be submitted with respective banks of prior intimation of at least 7 days from the date of attaining such milestone/landmark of construction progress.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">2.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">MODE OF PAYMENT</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">Subject to the terms of the Agreement and the DEVELOPER abiding by the construction milestones, the VENDEE/S shall make all payments, on written demand by the DEVELOPER, within the stipulated time as mentioned in the payment plan through A/c Payee cheque/demand draft/banker&#8217;s cheque or online payment in below mentioned account </span><span class="c5">Account bearing A/c. Nos 322205002425</span><span class="c4"> in favor of </span><span class="c5">M/s. ANANDA HOMES</span><span class="c4">, </span><span class="c5">Bank: ICICI BANK, Branch: MANIKONDA, IFSC: ICIC0003222.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">3.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">COMPLAINCE OF LAWS RELATING TO REMITTANCES</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">3.1 The VENDEE/S, if residents outside India, shall be solely responsible for complying with necessary formalities as laid down in Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999, Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934, and the Rules and Regulations made there-under or any statutory amendment(s) modification(s) made thereof and all other applicable laws including that of remittance of payment acquisition/sale/transfer of immovable properties in India, etc. and provide the DEVELOPER with such permission, approvals which would enable the DEVELOPER to fulfill its obligations under this Agreement. Any refund, transfer of security, if provided in terms of the Agreement shall be made in accordance with the provisions of Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999, or statutory enactments or amendments thereof and the Rules and Regulations of the Reserve Bank of India or any other applicable law. The VENDEE/S understand and agree that in the event of any failure on his/her part to comply with the applicable guidelines issued by the Reserve Bank of India, he/she may be liable for any action under the Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999, or other laws as applicable, as amended from time to time.</span></div>
<div class="c3x ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">3.2 The DEVELOPER accepts no responsibility in regard to matters specified in Para 3.1, above. The VENDEE/S shall keep the DEVELOPER fully indemnified and harmless in this regard. Whenever there is any change in the residential status of the VENDEE/S subsequent to the signing of this Agreement, it shall be the sole responsibility of the VENDEE/S to intimate the same in writing to the DEVELOPER immediately and comply with necessary formalities if any under the applicable laws. The DEVELOPER shall not be responsible towards any third-party making payment/remittances on behalf of any VENDEE/S and such third party shall not have any right in the application/allotment of the said flat applied herein in any way and the DEVELOPER shall be issuing the payment receipts in favor of the VENDEE/S only.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">4.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">ADJUSTMENT/APPROPRIATION OF PAYMENTS:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S authorizes the DEVELOPER to adjust/appropriate all payments made by him/her under any head(s) of dues against lawful outstanding of the VENDEE/S against the [Flat], if any, in his/her name and the VENDEE/S undertakes not to object/demand/direct the DEVELOPER to adjust his payments in any manner.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">5.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">TIME IS ESSENCE:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER shall abide by the time schedule for completing the project as disclosed at the time of registration of the project with the Authority and towards handing over the [Flats] to the VENDEE/S and the common areas to the association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be subject to the VENDEE/S make the payments as per the schedule mentioned above.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">6.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">CONSTRUCTION OF THE FLAT:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S have seen the sanction plan, specifications, amenities and facilities of the Schedule B Property and accepted floor plan, payment plan and the specifications, amenities and facilities (annexed along with this Agreement) which has been approved by the competent authority, as represented by the DEVELOPER. The DEVELOPER shall develop the Project in accordance with the said sanction plan or the modified plan, floor plans and specifications, amenities and facilities</span><span class="c5">. </span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2v">7.<span class="cm"></span><span class="c5">POSSESSION OF THE FLAT/PLOT:</span></div>
<div class="c3y"><span class="c4">7.1 Schedule for possession of the said [Flat]: The DEVELOPER agrees and understands that timely delivery of possession of the Schedule B property to the VENDEE/S and the common areas to the Association of VENDEE/S or competent authority, as the case may be, is the essence of the Agreement. The DEVELOPER assures to hand over possession of the Schedule B property of the project by June-2028&#8217; and with a grace period of 6 months unless there is a delay or failure due to war, flood, drought, fire, cyclone, earthquake, or any other calamity caused by nature or any Court stay or government order affecting the regular development of the real estate project (&#8220;Force Majeure&#8221;). If, however, the completion of the Project is delayed due to Force Majeure conditions then the VENDEE/S agree that the DEVELOPER shall be entitled to the extension of time and delivery of possession of the Schedule B property, provided that such Force Majeure conditions are not of nature which make it impossible for the contract to be implemented. The VENDEE/S agree and confirm that, in the event it becomes impossible for the DEVELOPER to implement the project due to Force Majeure conditions, then this agreement shall stand terminated and the DEVELOPER shall refund to the VENDEE, the entire amount received by the DEVELOPER from this agreement within 90 days from that date. The DEVELOPER shall intimate the VENDEE/S about such termination at least thirty days prior to such termination. After refund of the money paid to the VENDEE/S, the VENDEE/S agree that he/she shall not have any rights, claims, etc. against the DEVELOPER and that the DEVELOPER shall be released and discharged from all its obligations and liabilities under this Agreement.</span></div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">7.2 Procedure for taking possession &#8211; The Developers/Promoters (i) upon applying for and upon the completion of the period prescribed for issuing the Occupancy Certificate under applicable building laws; or (ii) after obtaining the Occupancy Certificate from the competent authority, shall offer in writing the possession of the Apartment, to the Vendee, who has paid all the amounts in terms of this Agreement. The Vendee shall take possession within two months from the date of the said notice. The Vendee shall be liable to pay property tax from the date of the Registration of the Sale Deed in favour of the Vendee or Occupancy Certificate whichever is earlier. </span></div>
<div class="cl ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">If the Vendee fails to take delivery within the time specified in the notice referred to in Clause 7.2 above, he shall be liable for payment of all on goings including maintenance charges, water and electricity charges, Corpus Fund etc. from the date of notice. The Vendee, after taking possession or in accordance with Clause 7.2, agrees to pay the maintenance charges as determined by the Developers/Association of Vendees.</span></div>
<div class="cp ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">7.3 Failure of VENDEE/S to take possession of Flat/Schedule B property &#8211; Upon receiving a written intimation from the DEVELOPER as per Para 7.2, the VENDEE/S shall take possession of the Flat from the documentation as prescribed in this Agreement, and the DEVELOPER shall give possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S. In case, the VENDEE/S fails to take possession within the time provided in para 7.2, such VENDEE/S shall continue to be liable to pay maintenance charges as specified in para 7.2.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">7.4</span><span class="c5"> </span><span class="c4">Possession by the VENDEE/S- After obtaining the occupancy certificate and handing over physical possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S, it shall be the responsibility of the DEVELOPER to hand over the necessary documents and plans, including common areas, to the Association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be, as per the local laws. [Provided that, in absence of any local law, the DEVELOPER shall handover the necessary documents and plans, including common areas, to the Association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be, within thirty days after obtaining the completion certificate]. Whereas it is made clear, that the VENDEE(S) / Purchaser shall be permitted for house-warming of his/her Flat subject to the payment/clearance of all the pending amounts due to the Developer and after obtaining No-Objection Certificate from Developer/Builder only.</span></div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">7.5 Cancellation by VENDEE/S &#8211; The Vendee shall have the right to cancel/withdraw his allotment in the Project only as provided in the Act.</span></div>
<div class="cl ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">Provided that, where the Vendee proposes to cancel/withdraw from the Project without any fault of the Developer/AGPA holder, the Developer/AGPA holder herein is entitled to deduct an amount of 10% of Total Sale Consideration towards penal charges or compensation/ damages from the amount collected by Developers /Promoters.&#160; &#160;</span></div>
<div class="c2d ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">The balance amount of money paid by the Vendee shall be returned by the&#160; &#160;Developer/AGPA holder to the Vendee within three months of such cancellation or at the time that the Developer/AGPA holder are able to resell the said Apartment to another purchaser, whichever is later.</span></div>
<div class="cp ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="cp"><span class="c4">&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;7.6 Transfer rights by Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s):</span></div>
<div class="c3z ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s) is/are not allowed to sell / re-sell /transfer/ alienate his rights or assign or otherwise nominate a third party in any manner whatsoever till Two years from the date of Agreement of sale or the project is completed in full, whichever is later.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The Vendee shall have the right to nominate one blood relative in whose name the Sale Deed for the Apartment can be registered instead of the Vendee, prior to the registration of the Sale Deed. This is limited to only a one-time nomination.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The Vendee hereby declares that he/she/they will not be entering into any kind of conveyances with third parties with respect to their apartment before the expiry of 24 months from the date of Agreement of Sale. In the event that, the Vendee seeks to transfer his rights concerning the Apartment at any time prior to the registration of the Sale Deed, he can only do so after the stipulated period of 24 months as mentioned here. The Vendee shall not sell the Apartment at any price lower than the prevailing base price of the Developer/AGPA holder for such Apartment and pay an amount of Rs. 150/- per SFT to the Developer/AGPA holder and obtain a No-objection Certificate from the Developer/AGPA holder with respect to such sale by executing required documentation between the Developer/AGPA holder, the Vendee and the third party. Any third party will be bound by the same condition in the event he intends to sell the Apartment. The third party that steps in as a result of such sale shall execute the relevant agreements in the same format as were executed by the Vendees with the Company and shall have all the obligations towards the Developer/AGPA holder as the Vendee had in the first instance.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The transfer of rights as described above is subject to the following conditions: (i) the Vendee having paid at least 20% of the total consideration from their own capital, and (ii) the Vendee has fulfilled and will full fill, until actual transfer of rights, all their contractual obligations as stipulated in this Agreement.</span></div>
<div class="c41"><span class="c40">7.7&#160; In the event the Developer fails to complete the construction of the Apartment and/or is unable to offer or deliver possession of the Apartment, duly completed in all respects, on or before the date stipulated in Clause 7.1, the Developer shall be liable to compensate the Allottee for such delay. The Developer shall pay compensation at the rate of Rs. 5/- (Rupees Five only) per square foot of the super built-up area per month of delay, calculated from the due date of possession until the actual date on which possession of the Apartment is handed over to the Allottee.</span></div>
<div class="c42"><span class="c5">8.</span><span class="c4"> </span><span class="c5">REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES OF THE DEVELOPER</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">8.1. The DEVELOPER hereby represents and warrant to the VENDEE/S as follows:</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(i)&#160; The DEVELOPER has absolute, clear and marketable title with respect to the said Land and the DEVELOPER has the requisite rights to carry out the development upon the said land and absolute, actual, physical and legal possession of the said Land for the Project.</span><span class="c43"></span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(ii) The DEVELOPER has lawful rights and requisite approvals from the competent authorities to carry out the development of the Project.</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(iii) The DEVELOPER has obtained Project Finance from &#8220;CAPRI GLOBAL CAPITAL LIMITED&#8221; Bank to carry out the development of the Project, by creating a charge on his share of the Constructed area in the Project, and it shall be the responsibility of the DEVELOPER to discharge the same.</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(iv)There is no litigations pending before any Court of law or Authority with respect to the said land or Project except those disclosed in the title report.</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(v)All approvals, licenses and permits issued by the competent authorities with respect to the Project, said Land and Schedule B Property are valid and subsisting and have been obtained by the following due process of law. Further, the DEVELOPER has been and shall, at all times, remain to be in compliance with all applicable laws in relation to the Project, said Land, Building and Schedule B property and common areas;</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(vi) The DEVELOPER has the right to enter into this Agreement and has not committed or omitted to perform any act or thing, whereby the right, title and interest of the VENDEE/S created herein, may be prejudicially affected.</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(vii) The DEVELOPER has not entered into any agreement for sale and/or development agreement or any other agreement/arrangement with any person or party with respect to the said Land, including the Project and the said Schedule B Property which will, in any manner, affect the rights of VENDEE/S under this Agreement.</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(viii) The DEVELOPER confirms that it is not restricted in any manner whatsoever from selling the said Schedule B Property to the VENDEE/S in the manner contemplated in this Agreement;</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(ix) At the time of execution of the Sale deed the DEVELOPER shall handover lawful, vacant, peaceful, physical possession of the Schedule B Property to the VENDEE/S and the common areas to the Association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be;</span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(x) The Developers/Promoters has duly paid and shall continue to pay and discharge all governmental dues, rates, charges and taxes and other monies, levies, impositions, premiums, damages and/or penalties and other outgoings, whatsoever, payable with respect to the said Project to the competent Authorities till the completion certificate has been issued and possession of Total Apartment Complex or building Complex, as the case may be, along with Common Areas (equipped with all the specifications, amenities and facilities) has been handed over to the Association of Vendees or the competent authority, as the case may be. However, any property tax attracted to the Vendee shall be borne by the Vendee only </span></div>
<div class="co"><span class="c4">(xi) No notice from the Government or any other local body or authority or any legislative enactment, government ordinance, order, notification (including any notice for acquisition or requisition of the said property) has been received by or served upon the DEVELOPER in respect of the said Land and/or the Project except those disclosed on the title report.</span></div>
<div class="c44">8.2<span class="c2x"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S with intention to bring all persons into whatsoever hands the Flat may come, hereby covenants with the DEVELOPER as follows:</span></div>
<div class="c45 ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(i)<span class="c38"></span><span class="c4">To maintain the Flat as the VENDEE/S own cost in good and tenantable repair and condition from the date that of possession of the Flat is taken and shall not suffer to be done anything in or to the building in which the Flat is taken and shall not do or suffer to be done anything in or to the building in which the Flat is situated which may be against the rules, regulations or bye-laws or change/alter or make addition in or to the building in which the Flat is situated and the Flat itself or any part thereof without the consent of the local authorities, if required.</span></div>
<div class="c47 ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(ii)<span class="c3b"></span><span class="c4">Not to store in the Flat, any goods, which are hazardous, combustible or dangerous nature or are so heavy as to damage the construction or structure of the building in which the Flat is situated or storing of which goods is objected to by the concerned local or other authority and shall take care while carrying heavy packages which may damage or likely to damage the staircases, common passages or any other structure of the building in which the Flat is situated, including the entrances of the building in which the Flat is situated and in case any damage is caused to the building in which the Flat is situated or the Flat on account of negligence or default of the VENDEE/S in this behalf, the VENDEE/S shall be liable for the consequences of the breach.</span></div>
<div class="c48 ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(iii)<span class="c3c"></span><span class="c4">To carry out at his own cost all internal repairs to the said Flat/Flat and maintain the Flat in the same condition, state and order in which it was delivered by the DEVELOPER to the VENDEE/S and shall not do or suffer to be done anything in or to the building in which the Flat is situated or the Flat which may be contrary to the rules and regulations and bye-laws of the concerned local authority or other public authority. In the event of the VENDEE/S committing any act in contravention of the above provision, the VENDEE/S shall be responsible and liable for the consequences thereof to the concerned local authority and/or other public authority.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(iv)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">Not to demolish or cause to be demolished the Flat or any part thereof, not at any time make or cause to be made any addition or alteration of whatever nature in or to the Flat or any part thereof, nor any alteration in the elevation and outside color scheme of the building in which the Flat is situated and shall keep the portion, sewers, drains and pipes in the Flat and the appurtenances thereto in good tenantable repair and condition, and in particular, so as to support shelter and protect the other parts of the building in which the Flat is situated and shall not chisel or in any other manner cause damage to columns, beams, walls, slabs or RCC Pardi or other structural members in the Flat without the prior written permission of the DEVELOPER and/or the Society or the Limited Company.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(v)<span class="c49"></span><span class="c4">Not to make any additional modifications to the Flat that may be visible from the outside which shall include without limitation putting of any Grills, walls or temporary structures and it is specifically agreed that in the event of any default by the Vendee, the Developer or the Society, as the case may be whoever are managing the common areas shall be entitled to remove the same and recover the costs from the Vendee.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(vi)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">Not to do or permit to be done any act or thing which may render void or voidable any insurance of the project land and the building in which the Flat is situated or any part thereof or whereby any increased premium shall become payable in respect of the insurance.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(vii)<span class="c4a"></span><span class="c4">Not to throw dirt, rubbish, rags, garbage or other refuse or permit the same to be thrown from the said Flat in the compound or any portion of the project land and the building in which the Flat is situated.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(viii)<span class="c4b"></span><span class="c4">Pay to the DEVELOPER within fifteen days of demand by the DEVELOPER, his share of security deposit demanded by the concerned local authority or Government for giving water, electricity, or any other service connection to the building in which the Flat is situated.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(ix)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">To bear and pay increase in the local taxes, water charges, insurance and such other levies, if any, which are imposed by the concerned local authority and/or Government and/or other public authority, on account of change of user of the Flat by the VENDEE/S for any purposes other than for the purpose for which it is sold.</span></div>
<div class="c48 ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(x)<span class="c49"></span><span class="c4">The VENDEE/S shall observe and perform all the rules and regulations which the Society or the Limited Company or Apex Body or Federation or Association may adopt at its inception and the additions, alterations or amendments thereof that may be made from time to time for protection and maintenance of the said building and the Flats therein and for the observance and performance of the Building rules, regulations and Bye-laws for the time being of the concerned local authority and of Government and other public bodies. The VENDEE/S shall also observe and perform all the stipulations and conditions laid down by the Society/Limited Company/Apex Body/Federation/Association regarding the occupancy and use of the Flat in the Building and shall pay and contribute regularly and punctually towards the taxes, expenses or other out-goings in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(xi)<span class="c3d"></span><span class="c4">Till a conveyance of the common areas, services and amenities of the building/project in which the Flat is situated is executed in favour of Society/Association and till all the total built-up area/units are sold off, the VENDEE/S shall permit the PROMOTER and their surveyors and agents, with or without workmen and others, at all reasonable times, to enter into and upon the said buildings or any part thereof to view and examine the state and condition thereof.</span></div>
<div class="c2s ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c46">(xii)<span class="c4a"></span><span class="c4">To pay the applicable Property Tax to GHMC / HMDA / such other statutory authority as may be applicable from, the date of registration of the Flat by the Developer to the Vendee, within the period specified.</span></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">9.EVENTS OF DEFAULTS AND CONSEQUENCES</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">9.1 Subject to the Force Majeure clause, the DEVELOPER shall be considered under a condition of default, in the following events:</span></div></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(i) DEVELOPER fails to provide ready to move in possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S within the time period specified in para 7.1 or fails to complete the project within the stipulated time disclosed at the time of registration of the project with the Authority. For the purpose of this Para, ready to move in possession&#8217; shall mean that the flat shall be in a habitable condition which is complete in all respects including the provision of all specifications, and facilities, as agreed to between the parties, and for which occupation certificate as the case may be, has been issued by the competent authority.</span></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(ii) Discontinuance of the DEVELOPER business as a developer on account of suspension or revocation of his registration under the provisions of the Act or the rules and regulations made there under.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">9.2 In case of Default by the DEVELOPER under the conditions listed above, VENDEE/S are entitled to the following:</span></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(i) Stop making further payments to the DEVELOPER as demanded by the DEVELOPER. If the VENDEE/S stop making payments, the DEVELOPER shall correct the situation by completing the construction milestones and only thereafter the VENDEE/S be required to make the next payment without any interest, or</span></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(ii) The VENDEE/S shall have the option of terminating the Agreement in which case the DEVELOPER shall be liable to refund the entire money paid by the VENDEE/S under any head whatsoever towards the purchase of the flat, along with interest at the rate prescribed in the rules within ninety days of receiving the termination: Provided that where an VENDEE/S does not intend to withdraw from the project or terminate the Agreement, he shall be paid, by the DEVELOPER, interest at the rate prescribed in the Rules, for every month of delay till the handing over of the possession of the Flat, which shall be paid by the DEVELOPER to the VENDEE/S within ninety days of it becoming due.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">9.3 The VENDEE/S shall be considered under a condition of Default, on the occurrence of the following events:</span></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(i) In case the VENDEE fails to make payments for 1(One) consecutive demands made by the DEVELOPER as per the Payment Plan annexed hereto, despite having been issued notice in that regard the VENDEE shall be liable to pay interest to the DEVELOPER on the unpaid amount at the rate prescribed in the Rules;</span></div>
<div class="c3a"><span class="c4">(ii) In case of default by VENDEE/S under the condition listed above continues for a period beyond 1 (one) consecutive month after notice from the DEVELOPER in this regard, the DEVELOPER may cancel the allotment of Schedule B property in favor of the VENDEE/S and refund the money paid to him by the VENDEE/S by deducting the booking amount and the interest liabilities and this Agreement shall thereupon stand terminated. Provided that the DEVELOPER shall intimate the VENDEE/S about such termination at least thirty days prior to such termination. The amount shall be repaid by the DEVELOPER within a period of ninety days after termination or the date on which the DEVELOPER able to resell the Schedule B Property to other VENDEE/S, whichever is later.</span></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">10. CONVEYANCE OF THE SAID FLAT:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER, on receipt of total price of the Flat per para 1.1 under the Agreement from the VENDEE/S, shall execute a conveyance deed / sale Deed and convey title of the flat together with proportionate indivisible share in the common areas within 3 months from the date of issuance of the occupancy certificate and the completion certificate, as the case may be, to the VENDEE/S. However, in case the VENDEE/S fails to deposit the stamp duty and/or registration charges within the period mentioned in the notice, the DEVELOPER shall hold the registration till the payment of stamp duty and registration charges to the DEVELOPER is made by the VENDEE/S.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">11. MAINTENANCE OF THE SAID BUILDING/FLAT:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.1 The DEVELOPER shall be responsible to provide and maintain essential service in the Project till the taking over or the maintenance of the Project by the Association of VENDEE/S and the cost of maintenance shall be borne by the DEVELOPER and the VENDEE/S, proportionate to the Flats in their respective occupation, provided that the Promoter shall exclusively provide the maintenance services for the Flat till the date on which the Flat is handed over to the VENDEE. After such period, the Association of VENDEE/S shall be responsible for the maintenance of the Flat and Project. The VENDEE/S further agree that the Developer shall be permitted to appoint a Property Management Company (&#8220;PMC&#8221;) for the maintenance. The VENDEE/S agree to enter into a Property Management Agreement with the PMC in the form prescribed by the DEVELOPER/PMC in relation to the provision of such services as and when asked by the DEVELOPER.</span></div></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.2 The facilities like club house and service connections, like water and sewerage supply, which are common shall be maintained by the DEVEOPER till the entire project is completed. The club house and its services shall be subject to user charges as may be fixed by the DEVELOPER of the club house or as the case may be the service provider, from time to time.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.3 All other infrastructural facilities, including the equipment like lift, mechanical, electrical or electronic equipment, STP, etc shall be covered by appropriate annual maintenance agreements and insurance agreements with the authorized service providers and the costs of such annual maintenance charges and insurance shall be part of the maintenance charges payable by the occupants. Unless the possession is delivered to the VENDEE, the DEVELOPER shall be the occupant in respect of the flats/buildings in the project.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.4 The DEVELPOR/maintenance agency/Association or VENDEE/S shall have right of unrestricted access of all Common areas, covered parking and other parking spaces for providing necessary maintenance services and the VENDEE/S agree to permit the Association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency to enter into the Flat or any part thereof, after due notice and during the normal working hours, unless the circumstances warrant otherwise, with a view to set right any defect.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.5 VENDEE/S shall have to pay monthly subscriptions as user charges for various facilities such as Club House, Gym, Swimming Pool, and other specific facilities, etc. to be decided by the DEVELOPER at the time of commencement of Maintenance period.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.6 DEVELOPER reserves the right to appoint the various service providers for the given amenities including the duration of such appointments, in the interest of the community. The VENDEE/S hereby agree to abide by the bye-laws of the society, club rules and regulations and shall be liable for all such rules and regulations mentioned in the bye-laws, scope of maintenance and shall support all such amendments to the bye-laws from time to time. Scope of Maintenance as per Schedule E</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.7 It is agreed by the VENDEE/S that he/she/they shall alone be liable to pay the maintenance charges, irrespective of whether the Flat is occupied or not or occupied by a tenant or any other person. THE Society shall have charge on every Flat for all amounts including the maintenance charges, due from the VENDEE/S or other occupants.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.8 During the execution of interiors, the VENDEE/S hereby agree to pay charges towards Debris for a single clearance, fixed electricity charges and also agree to pay towards expenses for maintenance of common areas, till the commencement of pre-paid maintenance. All these payments shall be made either in the name of the DEVELOPER or its nominee.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">11.9 The DEVELOPER reserves the right to maintain the common areas of the community for initial two years from the date of commencement of pre-paid maintenance. The commencement date will be intimated and informed either by the company or its nominee. The VENDEE/S hereby agree to pay an amount of Rs. 4/- per</span><span class="c5"> </span><span class="c4">Sft for a period of 2 years on the saleable area of his flat as maintenance and corpus fund charges for common areas and all other facilities (the club house maintenance charges are excluded), payable on demand made by the DEVELOPER, normally &#8216;1&#8217; months before handing over of the flat. The DEVELOPER is also free to increase the charges if the above-mentioned amount does not cover the maintenance expenses of the building.</span></div>
<div class="ci"><span class="c4">12</span><span class="c5">. DEFECT LIABILITY</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">12.1 It is agreed that in case any structural defect or any other defect in workmanship, quality or provision of services or any other obligations (excluding the under-mentioned in clause no.2) of the DEVELOPER as per the agreement for sale relating to such development is brought to the notice of the DEVELOPER within a period of 5 (five) years by the VENDEE/S from the date of handing over possession, it shall be the duty of the DEVELOPER to rectify such defects without further charge, within 30 (thirty) days, and in the event of DEVELOPER failure to rectify such defects within such time, the aggrieved VENDEE/S shall be entitled to receive appropriate compensation in the manner as provided under the Act.</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">12.2. Notwithstanding anything contained in the above clause the following exclusions are made</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">a. Equipment (passenger/goods, lifts, generator, motors, STP, transformers, gym equipment, windows, etc.) which carry manufacturer&#8217;s guarantees for a limited period. Thereafter, the welfare association/society shall take annual maintenance contract with the suppliers. The DEVELOPER shall transfer manufacturer&#8217;s guarantees/warrantees to the VENDEE/S or association of VENDEE/S as the case may be.</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">b. Fittings related to plumbing, sanitary, electrical switches, public bath fitting, door hardware, etc. having natural wear and tear.</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">c. Allowable structural and other deformations including expansion quotient (Tiles, granite, railing, wood doors and Kitchen sink).</span></div>
<div class="c4d"><span class="c4">d. The terms of work like painting etc. which are subject to wear and tear.</span></div>
<div class="c4c"><span class="c4">12.3. The VENDEE/S shall maintain the flats in good tenantable conditions and carry out the internal repairs for the upkeep of the flats. The association of the VENDEE/S or its assigns shall maintain the services and amenities in good condition and covered with proper AMC and insurance. The obligation of the promoter shall be subject to proper maintenance and upkeep of the flats/services and amenities by the VENDEE/S or the association of VENDEE/S as the case may be.</span></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">13. RIGHT TO ENTER THE FLAT FOR REPAIRS</span><span class="c4">:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER/maintenance agency/association of VENDEE/S shall have rights of unrestricted access of all common areas, garages/covered parking and parking spaces for providing necessary maintenance services and the VENDEE/S agree to permit the association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency to enter into the Schedule B property or any part thereof, after due notice and during the normal working hours, unless the circumstances warrant otherwise, with a view to set right any defect.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">14.USAGE:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">Use of Basement and Service Areas: The basement(s) and service areas, if any, as located within the flats shall be earmarked for purposes such as parking spaces and services including but not limited to electric sub-station, transformer, DG set rooms, underground water tanks, pump rooms, maintenance and service rooms, firefighting and equipment&#8217;s etc and other permitted uses as per plans. The VENDEE/S shall not be permitted to use the services areas and the basements in any manner whatsoever, other than those earmarked as parking formed by the VENDEE/S for rendering maintenance services.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">15.GENERAL COMPLAINCE WITH RESPECT TO THE FLAT:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.1 Subject to Para 12 above, the VENDEE/S shall, after taking possession, be solely responsible to maintain the Schedule B property at his/her/its own cost, in good repair and condition and shall not do or suffer to be done anything in or to the Building, or the Schedule B property or the staircases, lifts, common passages, corridors, circulation areas, atrium or the compound which may be in violation of any laws or rules of any authority or change or alter or make additions to the Schedule B property and keep the Schedule B property, its walls and partitions, sewers, drains, pipe and appurtenances thereto or belonging thereto, in good and tenantable repair and maintain the same in a fit and proper condition and ensure that the support, shelter, etc. of the Building is not in any way damaged or jeopardized.</span></div></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.2 The VENDEE/S further undertake, assure and guarantee that he/she would not put any sign-based/name play, neon light, publicity material or advertisement material etc. on the face/fa&#231;ade of the building or anywhere on the exterior of the Project, buildings therein or common areas. The VENDEE/S shall also not change the color scheme of the outer walls or painting of the exterior side of the window or carry out any change in the exterior elevation or design. Further, the VENDEE/S shall not store any hazardous or combustible goods in Schedule B property or place any heavy material in the common passages or staircase of the building. The VENDEE/S shall also not remove any wall, including the outer and load bearing wall of the Schedule B property.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.3 The VENDEE/S shall plan and distribute its electrical load in conformity with the electrical systems installed by the DEVELOPER and thereafter the Association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency appointed by Association of VENDEE/S. The VENDEE/S shall be responsible for any loss or damages arising out of breach of any of the aforesaid conditions. </span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.4 The VENDEE/S shall pay user charges in respect of the Clubhouse, Gym, Swimming pool and all other facilities mentioned in Schedule-D annexed hereto provided by the DEVELOPER or to its nominee or to the Society as per the usage under the Clubhouse rules and regulations and other notices given from time to time. Such user charges shall be paid to the DEVELOPER or its nominees who are the core service providers.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.5 Any type of modifications, changes, variations and alterations to the structural, elevation and architectural features shall not be permitted as the construction has been done using Shear Wall Technology and changes shall cause structural damage.</span><span class="c5"> </span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.6 The VENDEE/S shall not, at any time, demolish or be a cause to demolish their Flat or any part of the building including the common areas such as staircase, Verandah, parking places, etc. which are likely to cause injury or damage to the structure of the building. The VENDEE/S shall not make or be a cause to make any additions or alterations or any new connections of any nature, whatsoever, contrary to the plan for their Flat or to any part of the building. The VENDEE/S shall not close the balconies and parking with grills or any other partitions or fix sliding/fixed windows to the balconies/service areas or make any additions and alterations in the elevation and shall not alter the exterior of the building, including color scheme without the unanimous approval of the Association.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.7 The VENDEE/S shall keep their Flat as well as partition walls, drains, drainpipes, water pipelines and the appurtenances thereto in good tenable condition so as to support shelter and protect all parts of the building and also for good utility and occupation.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.8 The VENDEE/S shall use the common over-head tank provided for, along with other Flat owners of the building, and agree to pay the water charges as and when levied, proportionately as per the reading of water meter. The VENDEE/S agree to fix the air conditioner units, both the outdoor and indoor units at the designated location as shown/earmarked in the flat only. The VENDEE/S cannot request for the same to be shifted for any reason.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.9 The VENDEE/S also covenants that they will not throw dust, rubbish, rags, waste, spit or permit the same to be thrown in the compound or in any portion of the said building which may cause damage or inconvenience to other occupants of the building. It is hereby specifically agreed by the VENDEE/S that will dry their clothes only in the Utility areas. The VENDEE/S will not dry any clothes on the parapet walls of Utility area or utilize common areas such as the terrace to dry their clothes and are required to use specifically designed stand/apparatus/pulley systems for the same. The VENDEE/S shall not keep door mats, shoe racks, footwear or any kind of personal material or their belongings in any of the common areas including the corridors, parking areas, terrace areas, etc.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.10. The VENDEE/S and Association of VENDEE/S agree not to dry clothes in the Sit out, place pots, clad the walls in any material, paint the walls in a different colour, install false ceiling in Balcony, fix cupboard/racks or make any modifications to the Sit outs. The DEVELOPER reserves the right to remove any such installations/modifications at any point of time till the complete hand over of the project to the Association.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.11. The VENDEE/S or Association of VENDEE/S agree that corridor area will not be used fix cupboards</span><span class="c5">, </span><span class="c4">shoe rack, racks, place pots or undertake any modification to the way it was handed over. Further, the VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES agree that no changes to the main door including change in color, height and width, installation of additional screen door over the main door will be undertaken by them. The VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES also agree that corridor walls including those next to the main door will not be painted in a different color, cladded with material or make any necessary changes to the way it is handed over at time of completion.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.12. The VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES agree that their name board outside their flat will be in accordance to the design provided by the DEVELOPER. Further they agree that no light fixtures or signages can be installed outside the main door or corridor.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.13. The VENDEE/S hereby agree that they will use the said Flat for residential purposes only and shall not use for commercial purposes such as office space, clinics, consultancies, display centers, service flats. or permit the same to be used for any other purpose which may likely to cause inconvenience to the neighboring occupants of the building nor shall it be used for any illegal or immoral purposes but strictly for residential use and if it is let out, should be utilized for the residential purpose only.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.14. It is agreed between the parties that the Area shown in the Schedule B as a Verandah</span><span class="c5"> </span><span class="c4">area attached to the entrance of the Flat shall be for the exclusive utilization of the VENDEE/S and no third parties shall be allowed to utilize the same without the express authorization of the VENDEE/S. However, it is specifically agreed by the VENDEES that this &#8220;Sit-Out&#8221; area shall not be covered or barricaded in any manner. Provided that, in the event that the VENDEE/S are particularly of the intent to cover / barricade the area, the same may be permitted by the Owners&#8217; Association that is in charge of the maintenance of the Project, on collection of a sum of not less than Rs. 20,00,000/- (Rupees Twenty Lakhs only), as may be stipulated by the Association and all and any such amounts received shall be remitted into the Corpus Account of the Project, for being utilized as such, for such purposes that the Corpus amounts may be utilized.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">Planter boxes and windows are staggered and positioned differently for each Flat and they will be fixed as per the architectural elevation design.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">15.15 Plants to be planted in the planted box will be defined by the DEVELOPER and has to be strictly followed by the VENDEE/S.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">16.COMPLIANCE OF LAWS, NOTIFICATIONS ETC.BY PARTIES:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The Parties are entering into this Agreement for the allotment of a Schedule B Property with the full knowledge of all laws, rules, regulations, notifications applicable to the project.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">17.ADDITIONAL CONSTRUCTIONS:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">The DEVELOPER undertake that they have no right to make additions or to out up additional structure(s) anywhere in the Project after the building plan, layout plan, sanction plan and specifications, amenities and facilities have been approved by the competent authority(ies) and disclosed, except for as provided in the Act, except as already informed to the VENDEE/S and set out in this Agreement.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">18. MORTGAGE OR CREATE A CHARGE:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">Notwithstanding any other term of this Agreement, the VENDEE/S hereby authorizes and permits the DEVELOPER to raise finance/loan from bank</span><span class="c5">, </span><span class="c4">by way of charge/mortgage/securitization of the Flat/Project/Building or the land underneath or the receivables, subject to the condition that the Flat shall be made free from all encumbrances at the time of execution of Sale deed shall be done in favor of the VENDEE/S or shall seek No Objection from &#8220;Bank&#8221; before execution of Agreement in respect the Schedule B property in favor of the VENDEE/S shall be informed about the same at the time of the agreement.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="ci"><span class="c5">19. MISCELLANEOUS:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.1 The Parties hereby agree that in case the VENDEE/S are availing a housing loan/loan from any bank/Financial institution/Non-Banking Financial Corporation Financier (the &#8220;Bank&#8221;), a Tri-partite Agreement, as per the draft provided by the Bank and agreed by the DEVELOPER shall be executed by and between the Bank, the DEVELOPER and the VENDEE/S. In any event, the VENDEE/S will finance the margin money, and the loan will be paid directly from the Bank to the DEVELOPER. The VENDEE/S acknowledge that the VENDEE/S obligation to pay the total sale consideration as mentioned in this Agreement shall be independent and exclusive liability, which is independent of the bank loan obtained by the VENDEE/S, such that, if the VENDEE/S are unable to obtain a bank loan or having obtained a bank loan, the Bank is not disbursing the money, the VENDEE/S SHALL be independently liable to pay the sale consideration to the DEVELOPER. The DEVELOPER shall not be responsible in any way if the VENDEE/S do not succeed in receiving a loan from the Bank.</span></div></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.2. The building is named and called as </span><span class="c5">&#8220;THE LEGACEY&#8221; </span><span class="c4">and the DEVELOPER can erect display boards/name boards as per their commercial and branding requirements on a permanent basis. The name board of the builders will be displayed permanently at the site and the VENDEE/S have no objection to the same.</span></div>
<div class="cl"><span class="c4">19.3 </span><span class="c4e">Whereas the Vendee was clearly informed and acknowledges that the Developer has applied for permission to construct two additional floors, i.e., the 23rd and 24th floors, above the sanctioned Ground + 22 floors, by utilizing Transferable Development Rights (TDR) purchased by the Developer.&#160; The Vendee agrees that the said additional floors (23rd and 24th floors), shall be the exclusive property of the Developer, and the Vendee shall have no right, title, interest, or claim of any nature whatsoever in respect thereof. The Vendee further has no objection to the allocation and distribution of the proportionate undivided share of land among the purchasers/owners of the sanctioned Ground + 22 floors, as may be finalized upon approval of the revised plan by the competent authority. The Vendee undertakes to sign and furnish all documents required by competent authorities, for obtaining approvals, sanctions, for the said additional floors, without objection to the developer.</span></div>
<div class="cl ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.4 The VENDEE/S will not be allowed to start interior works until the construction of flat is totally constructed and completed. Once, the flat is handed over to the VENDEE/S for interiors means and includes that the flat is fully finished and formalities of handover is complete, irrespective of whether or not the flat is ready for living. Interiors will be allowed only after handing over/taking over of the Flat. The Interiors shall be done between 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM only. THE VENDEE/S has to pay a penalty to the society for interiors done beyond 4 months of handing over.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.5 The Developer/Promoter reserves the right to maintain the common areas of the community for initial two years from the date of commencement of pre-paid maintenance. The commencement date will be notified either by the Developer or its nominee at an appropriate time. The purchaser hereby agrees to pay an amount of Rs.96/- per Sq. Ft. Plus 18% GST for the saleable area as maintenance charges for maintenance of common areas for the period of two (2) years. The Water charges are NOT included in the said maintenance charges. (payable on demand made by the developer, normally '3' months before handing over). During the execution of interiors, the purchaser/s hereby agree/s to pay the fixed one-time Move in charges @ Rs.25,000/- Plus 18% GST; towards clearance of debris, Fixed Electricity charges during for 3 Months from the date of Possession, thereafter the charges for Electricity shall be applicable based on units consumed as per the electric meter reading. The Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s) also agrees to pay Rs. 2/- per Sq. Ft. plus 18% GST of the saleable area per month, on monthly basis, towards interim maintenance of common areas and utilities, till such time of commencement of pre-paid maintenance for two years. This interim maintenance is payable irrespective of completion of interior works and all these payments shall be made either in the name of developer or its nominee. The VENDEE/S shall pay an amount of Rs. 25,000/- plus 18% GST towards legal and documentation charges plus applicable taxes at the time of execution of Sale Deed Registration.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">If any water problem arises due to insufficient depth of the present bore well, the VENDEE(S) hereby agreed to share proportionately the expenses/cost incurred for increasing the depth of the present Bore-well or for digging new Bore-well. The Developer will not be responsible for the same and all the Flat Owners of the building shall collectively bear the same.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.6 It is agreed that the parking places will be allotted to the VENDEE/S through the lottery method.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.7&#160; It is agreed by both the parties that the Developer will provide CCTV surveillance only for drive ways , entry &amp; exit ramps of parking area. No individual parking slots will be covered by CCTV.</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">19.8 All the owners/residents must park their vehicles in the parking lots allotted to them and they must not park their vehicles in any of the open areas of the building, setbacks, or in the parking lots of other owners/residents.</span></div>
<div class="ci"><span class="c5">20. The DEVELOPER shall take the following steps to enable formation of an Association of VENDEE/S under S.11(4)(e) of the Act:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">With respect to a real estate project, the DEVELOPER shall submit an application to the Registrar for registration of the Association of VENDEE/S as a society under the Telangana/A.P Societies Registration Act, 2001 (as applicable to the state of Telangana), within two months from the date on which the occupation certificate in respect of such project is issued and a minimum of sixty per cent of the total VENDEE/S in such a project have taken possession and the DEVELOPER has received the full consideration from such VENDEE/S. All the VENDEE/S on payment of full consideration shall become members of such Association of VENDEE/S formed by the DEVELOPER applications, petitions, for forming an association.</span></div>
<div class="c2k">a)<span class="c2l"></span><span class="c4">The Association will have to be formed as per the above clause, however, the decision with regard to continuation of maintenance by the PROMOTER/DEVELOPER, will be at that point of time vest with the Association. If the DEVELOPER fails to form the Association of VENDEE/S, the Authority shall by an order direct the DEVELOPER to apply for formation of such Association or may authorize the VENDEE/S to apply for the formation of the said Association.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
<div class="c2k">b)<span class="c2l"></span><span class="c4">Notwithstanding any other rule, after conveying the title to the Association of VENDEE/S under S.17, the DEVELOPER shall continue to have the rights and entitlement to advertise, market, book, sell or offer to sell or allot to person to purchase any flat or building or plot which is still not sold or allotted and shall be deemed to have been allowed to do so by the Association of DEVELOPER without any restriction or entry of the building and development of common areas.</span></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="c2u"><span class="c5">21. ENTIRE AGREEMENT:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">This Agreement along with its schedules, constitutes the entire Agreement between the parties with respect to the subject-matter hereof and supersedes any and all understandings, any other agreements, allotment letter, correspondences, arrangements, whether written or oral, if any, between the Parties in regard to the said Schedule B Property, as the case may be.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="c2u"><span class="c5">22.RIGHT TO AMEND:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">This Agreement may only be amended through written consent of Both the Parties.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="c2u"><span class="c5">23. PROVISIONS OF THIS AGREEMENT APPLICABLE ON VENDEE/S/SUBSEQUENT VENDEE/S:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">It is clearly understood and so agreed by and between the Parties hereto that all the provisions contained herein and the obligations arising hereunder in respect of the Schedule B property and the Project shall equally be applicable to and enforceable against and by any subsequent VENDEE/S of Schedule B property, in case of a transfer, as the said obligations go along with the Schedule B Property for all intents and purposes.</span></div></div>
<div class="ag-keep"><div class="c2u"><span class="c5">24. WAIVER NOT A LIMITATION TO ENFORCE:</span></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">24.1 The DEVELOPER may, at its sole option and discretion, without prejudice to its rights as set out in this Agreement, waive the breach by the VENDEE/S in not making the payments as per the Payment Plan [Schedule C] including waiving the payment of interest for delayed payment. It is made clear and so agreed by the VENDEE/S that exercise of discretion by the DEVELOPER in the case of one VENDEE shall not be construed to be a precedent and/or binding on the DEVELOPER to exercise such discretion in the case of other VENDEE/S.</span></div></div>
<div class="ch"><span class="c4">24.2 Failure on the part of the Parties to enforce at any time or for any period of time the provisions hereof shall not be construed to be a waiver of any provisions or of the right thereafter to enforce each and every provision.</span></div>
<div class="ch ag-tight">&#160;</div>
